<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data Moshakha collects, why we collect it, who we share it with, and the choices and rights you have over it."
  canonical="/privacy-policy"
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information Moshakha ("we", "us") collects when you visit
    <strong>www.moshakha.com</strong>, why we collect it, and what control you have over it.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not sell personal information. We collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics data.</strong> If analytics is enabled, we use Google Analytics 4 to
      understand which pages people read. This records pages viewed, approximate location
      (country/region level), device and browser type, and referring site. IP addresses are
      anonymised by Google before storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you send us.</strong> If you email us, we receive whatever you choose
      to include in that message. We use it to reply and nothing else.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect payment details — no transaction ever takes place on this site.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics cookies are used only to produce aggregate traffic statistics. Affiliate
    partners, principally Amazon, may set their own cookies once you click through to their
    site so they can attribute a sale. Those cookies are governed by that partner's privacy
    policy, not ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time. The site works
    normally without them.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — traffic measurement. See Google's privacy policy.</li>
    <li><strong>Amazon Associates</strong> — affiliate attribution when you click through to Amazon.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — hosting. GitHub processes standard server request logs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not share, rent or sell your information to anyone else.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete the
    personal information we hold about you, and to object to its processing. Because we hold
    almost nothing tied to you personally, this is usually limited to email correspondence.
    Contact us and we will act on the request.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can opt out of Google Analytics entirely using Google's browser add-on, or by blocking
    analytics cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information
    from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, we will update the date at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions can be sent via our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
